Input: {"question": "In which significant event was HMS Penylan involved?", "source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 15, "text": "**HMS Penylan**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 17, "end": 96, "text": "HMS Penylan was a Hunt-class destroyer of the Royal Navy, commissioned in 1942."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 97, "end": 237, "text": "This article provides comprehensive evidence for the statement that HMS Penylan was involved in the significant event of ship commissioning."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 238, "end": 272, "text": "**Early History and Construction**"}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 274, "end": 352, "text": "HMS Penylan was built by the shipyard of Cammell Laird at Birkenhead, England."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 353, "end": 437, "text": "The ship's keel was laid down on 4 June 1941, and she was launched on 10 March 1942."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 438, "end": 551, "text": "[1] The construction of HMS Penylan was part of the Royal Navy's efforts to expand its fleet during World War II."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 552, "end": 578, "text": "**Commissioning Ceremony**"}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 580, "end": 703, "text": "On 25 August 1942, HMS Penylan was commissioned into the Royal Navy, marking a significant milestone in the ship's history."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 704, "end": 832, "text": "[2] The commissioning ceremony is a formal act that places a ship in active service, and it is a crucial event in a ship's life."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 833, "end": 993, "text": "The ceremony typically involves the raising of the ship's colors, the reading of the commissioning warrant, and the assumption of command by the ship's captain."}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 994, "end": 1023, "text": "**Evidence of Commissioning**"}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1025, "end": 1153, "text": "The commissioning of HMS Penylan is documented in various sources, including the ship's logbook and official Royal Navy records."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1154, "end": 1339, "text": "According to the logbook, the ship's company assembled on the quarterdeck on 25 August 1942, where the commissioning warrant was read by the ship's captain, Lieutenant Commander John M."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1340, "end": 1347, "text": "Hodges."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1348, "end": 1485, "text": "[3] The logbook also records the details of the ceremony, including the raising of the White Ensign and the National Anthem being played."}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1486, "end": 1506, "text": "**Credible Sources**"}, "D1S18": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1508, "end": 1585, "text": "The commissioning of HMS Penylan is supported by credible sources, including:"}, "D1S19": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1587, "end": 1696, "text": "* The Royal Navy's official records, which confirm the ship's commissioning date and details of the ceremony."}, "D1S20": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1697, "end": 1700, "text": "[2]"}, "D1S21": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1701, "end": 1788, "text": "* The ship's logbook, which provides a firsthand account of the commissioning ceremony."}, "D1S22": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1789, "end": 1792, "text": "[3]"}, "D1S23": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1793, "end": 1933, "text": "* Historical accounts of the Hunt-class destroyers, which include HMS Penylan's commissioning as a significant event in the class's history."}, "D1S24": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1934, "end": 1937, "text": "[4]"}, "D1S25": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1939, "end": 1953, "text": "**Conclusion**"}, "D1S26": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1955, "end": 2099, "text": "In conclusion, the evidence presented in this article demonstrates that HMS Penylan was involved in the significant event of ship commissioning."}, "D1S27": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2100, "end": 2240, "text": "The commissioning ceremony, which took place on 25 August 1942, marked the formal entry of the ship into active service with the Royal Navy."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 11, "text": "HMS Penylan"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 13, "end": 161, "text": "HMS Penylan was a Hunt-class destroyer of the Royal Navy that played a pivotal role in the significant event of boundary change during World War II."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 162, "end": 175, "text": "Early Service"}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 176, "end": 187, "text": "-----------"}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 189, "end": 262, "text": "HMS Penylan was commissioned on 15 August 1942, at the height of the war."}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 263, "end": 403, "text": "Initially, she was assigned to the Mediterranean Fleet, where she participated in several convoy escort missions and anti-submarine patrols."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 404, "end": 428, "text": "Boundary Change Incident"}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 429, "end": 453, "text": "------------------------"}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 455, "end": 571, "text": "On 12 November 1942, HMS Penylan was tasked with escorting a convoy of supply ships through the Strait of Gibraltar."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 572, "end": 681, "text": "As the convoy approached the Spanish-Moroccan border, it was intercepted by a group of Vichy French warships."}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 682, "end": 757, "text": "In the ensuing standoff, HMS Penylan's commanding officer, Captain James R."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 758, "end": 892, "text": "Fletcher, negotiated a temporary boundary change with the French authorities, allowing the convoy to pass through the disputed waters."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 893, "end": 1104, "text": "This boundary change, known as the \"Penylan Protocol,\" marked a significant shift in the balance of power in the region, as it established a precedent for future negotiations between the Allies and Vichy France."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1105, "end": 1127, "text": "Studies and References"}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1128, "end": 1150, "text": "----------------------"}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1152, "end": 1229, "text": "* \"The Hunt-Class Destroyers in World War II\" by Lieutenant Commander John W."}, "D2S17": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1230, "end": 1412, "text": "Smith, USN (Ret.) (Naval Institute Press, 1995) - This study provides an in-depth analysis of the Hunt-class destroyers, including HMS Penylan's role in the boundary change incident."}, "D2S18": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1413, "end": 1483, "text": "* \"The Penylan Protocol: A Study of Boundary Change in Wartime\" by Dr."}, "D2S19": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1484, "end": 1492, "text": "Emily J."}, "D2S20": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1493, "end": 1541, "text": "Wilson (Journal of International Relations, Vol."}, "D2S21": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1542, "end